              "type": "Type"
            }
          ],
          "content": "While other artists had their models pose as mythological figures, Rembrandt as a rule chose a direct rendering of his model. In this etching an undressed woman seated on a chair is surrounded by all sorts of clothes. The gentleman’s hat is conspicuous: what is it doing near this nude woman, and how did it get there?"
        },
        {
          "type": "LinguisticObject",
          "classified_as": [
            {
